From 9408b4aa287205673e84e3052180f3913d38ea20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: panvk-luke <panvk-luke@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:21:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH panvk-kirin990 17/23] panvk/jm: submit kbase atoms
 asynchronously with dependencies

The kbase JM backend submitted every tiler and fragment job with its own
ioctl + poll() + read(), so the CPU blocked after each job and the GPU
went idle between jobs.  Port the async atom table from the kbase JM
reference backend:

 - add a 256-entry atom slot table, atom-number allocator and the
   per-context event drain loop;
 - add kbase_kmod_job_submit_dep() with BASE_JD_DEP_TYPE_DATA
   dependencies, and kbase_kmod_wait_atom()/atom_release();
 - chain every atom of a queue submission to the previous one so the
   whole submission executes back-to-back on the GPU;
 - arm output vk_syncs with panvk_kbase_sync_set_pending() instead of
   blocking the submit path, and resolve submit waits on the CPU;
 - implement vkQueueWaitIdle and a bounded queue drain at destruction;
 - log submit/atom/wait averages every 120 submissions.
